The second version fulfils the specification more precisely:

• It uses ROW_NUMBER() so it always returns exactly 5 rows per city, whereas the first query’s RANK() could return more than 5 companies if there are ties.

• The results table produced by 2result.sql includes the expected 20 rows (5 × 4 cities) and keeps the national‑average column complete for every row (no truncation).

Therefore, 2result.sql is the correct choice.

```plaintext
2result.sql
```